# CQ-07 · viewer-anchored
#
# Question: Is there a directional spatial fact anywhere in the corpus that does
#           not name the viewer its direction is relative to?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. "Left of" with no vantage point
#           is the ambiguity that makes an unvalidated scene description
#           unusable downstream; clause C5 is VSON's answer to it.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §2 clause C5; §3.3 (viewer anchoring); §5.7
# Form:     ASK — a conformant corpus answers false
# Note:     This is the headline competency question: the mandatory viewer is
#           the constraint the README's contribution list rests on, and a
#           corpus-wide ASK returning false is what makes that claim checkable
#           rather than asserted. It is a real corpus-wide question because the
#           loader gives each document its own namespace — a fact in one
#           document can never borrow a viewer from another.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

ASK {
  ?fact a vso:SpatialFact ; vso:directional ?direction .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?fact vso:viewer ?viewer }
}
